 "answer": "pgvector declares the `vector` type with `STORAGE = extended`, so Postgres stores it as a variable-length value that can be compressed and moved out of line (TOAST) when it's large. In `pg_type`, this shows up as `typstorage = 'x'`.\n\nI'm going from memory of the extension's SQL definitions and haven't checked the current source. You can confirm on your installed version with:\n\n```sql\nSELECT typname, typstorage FROM pg_type WHERE typname = 'vector';\n```",
